cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "A Prefactor Coefficient Law for the Gauss-Legendre AGM Algorithm"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: C. Wayne
date-released: 2026-09-22
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22896047"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/agm-prefactor-coefficient-law"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22896047"
abstract: >-
  This paper studies an exact fitted correction coefficient for consecutive
  lower Gauss-Legendre approximants. Using Brent's theta-function expansion,
  it proves that alpha_(n+1)/alpha_n^2 tends to one half and identifies the
  limit as a prefactor effect after cancellation of the doubly exponential
  error scale.
keywords:
  - Gauss-Legendre algorithm
  - arithmetic-geometric mean
  - operator coefficients
  - sequence acceleration
  - Aitken delta-squared process
  - prefactor asymptotics
  - Baker N-series
  - numerical analysis
